WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.469
-The president delivered
a primetime address last night

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.172
on the government shutdown that
he started over his border wall.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.741
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.777
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.014
This was Trump's first
Oval Office address.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.183
Normally,
that's a solemn occasion,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.318
and one of the weightiest things
a president does.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:22.121
But as usual, Trump found a way
to make it weird.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.723
After the speech,
he tweeted,

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.192
"Thank you.
So many nice comments

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.294
regarding my
Oval Office speech --

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.097
a very interesting
experience."

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:34.233
"A very interesting
experience"?

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:37.903
He reacted to addressing
the nation from the Oval Office

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:40.640
the same way my grandpa did
to tapas.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.709
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.944
Also, if it was
so interesting,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.280
why didn't you
open you eyes more?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.448
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:52.218
You could have fit 10 of yours
into one Pelosi.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.752
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:56.689
[ Distinct laughter ]

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.657
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:00.994
-I love jokes
about politics.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.064
It's a great joke.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.033
-Whoa, whoa.
I have a question.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.601
Andy...

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.902
Andy, what are you
doing out here?

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.904
-Oh, nothing. I just figured,
since "Closer Look"

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.906
is the thing from the show
everyone watches online,

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.441
I'd try to be in it
and get some views.

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.076
What's up, YouTube?

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.378
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:22.215
-Hey, people watch
this show live.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.550
-Eh.
-Just get out of here.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.486
-Watch "Brooklyn Nine-Nine"
on Thursday!

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.855
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.960
-Now everyone's gonna
want to do that.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.362
Now, it's worth
taking a step back

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.596
and remembering
how we got here.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:40.266
We all know the wall was
the most memorable promise

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.336
of Trump's campaign, and
refrained at all of his rallies.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.172
And no matter he much he talked
about building a physical wall,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.239
to many of his supporters,

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:49.375
the wall remained
an imaginary thing.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.578
We're at a weird point where
Trump is basically the last guy

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:53.646
who wants a wall.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.782
I mean, it's fun to chant
"Build the wall,"

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.217
but they didn't
expect it to happen

00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:00.086
any more than they expected
Trump to actually lock her up.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:03.156
If you go to a Mets game,
you chant "Let's go Mets,"

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.892
but you don't really
expect them to go.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:06.893
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.262
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.200
Which might explain why, early
on, there were so few details

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.701
about how the wall
would actually be built.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.303
In fact, it took a question
from a child in the crowd

00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:20.039
at one of Trump's rallies
in 2015

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.842
to find out what the wall
would even be made of.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.377
First, here's the question --

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.813
-Okay. A young man --
come on. Young guy.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:30.583
-So, you're going to
build the wall.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.651
What's it going
to be made out of?

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:34.220
-Oh.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.588
-[ Mockingly ] "Oh."

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.023
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:41.928
"Oh, [bleep]. Why did I
let a kid ask a question?"

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.630
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.603
I will say -- I hate
watching Trump be president,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.804
but I would love
watching a show

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.573
where kids get to
ask him questions.

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:57.610
[ High-pitched voice ]
"Mr. Trump, where do
people go when they die?"

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.345
-They're going to China.
They're going to Japan.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.647
They're going
all over the place.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:03.750
"Grandpa's in Japan!"

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.020
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.323
[ Normal voice ]
But amazingly, the exchange
with Trump gets weirder,

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.391
because Trump then
invited the kid on stage

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:14.860
to repeat his question
while holding him up to the mic.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.696
And eventually,
Trump gave him an answer.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.698
-Lift him up here.
Bring him up here.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.732
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.834
Come on.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:27.106
-What -- what are the walls
going to be made...?

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.707
-Go ahead.
Ask it.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:31.878
-What are the walls
going to be made out of?

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:34.446
-I'll tell you what it's
gonna be made of.

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:36.449
It's gonna be made
of hardened concrete,

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.852
and it's gonna be made out of
rebar and steel.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.255
-Why does he hold
the kid up like that?

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.790
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:47.827
That kid's face looks like he's
being carried away by a falcon.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.029
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.197
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.899
So...

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.566
[ Applause ]

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:55.835
...Trump said very clearly

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.469
the wall would be made
from concrete.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:03:59.004
In fact,
as the campaign went on,

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:00.339
and even after
he became president,

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:02.708
he made lots of specific
promises about the wall --

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.243
who would pay for it,
what we should call it,

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.611
and how high it would be.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.913
He also repeatedly floated
a price tag for the wall --

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.949
a price tag that
seemed to change

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.284
basically any time
he opened his mouth.

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:15.988
-So, let's say it costs
$4 billion or $5 billion.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:19.024
So, if the wall costs
$6 billion to build...

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:23.429
You mean to tell me I can't take
$7 billion and build a wall?

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.297
Well, it's probably
$8 billion.

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.734
The wall is $10 billion
to $12 billion.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:32.171
I think for $18 billion or less,
we're gonna have a great wall.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.574
We're talking about a wall
for $20 billion.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:37.276
And they did agree to
a $25 billion wall.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:38.644
-He's a like a rich guy

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.779
yelling from the
"Price Is Right" audience

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.715
who doesn't know
how much things cost.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:46.752
"How much is this detergent?"
"3 billion. $3 billion."

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:48.821
Trump just made stuff up
off the top of his head

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.756
because the wall
was a ridiculous thing

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:52.592
he never thought he'd actually
have to build.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.060
At any point in
the last two years,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.762
Republicans -- who controlled
the House and Senate --

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.296
could have given Trump
money for the wall,

00:04:57.296 --> 00:05:00.032
but the didn't, because
it was obviously insane.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:02.434
And now, in his desperation
to get a deal,

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.303
he's throwing out everything
he said about the wall

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.506
on the campaign trail -- from
the fact that Mexico would pay

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:09.408
for 100% of it, to the fact that
it would be made of concrete,

00:05:09.408 --> 00:05:12.311
to the fact that it had to
be called a "wall."

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:14.880
-You ran your campaign
promising supporters

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.715
that Mexico was going to
pay for the wall...

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:19.285
-Oh, here we go again.
-...and that the wall was
going to be made of concrete.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.519
-I said I was gonna
build a wall.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.288
I never said
"I'm gonna build a concrete --"

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.589
I said
"I'm gonna build a wall."

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.290
Just so you don't --
'cause I know you're not into

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:29.728
the construction business --
steel is stronger than concrete.

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:32.765
If I build this wall,
or fence,

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.535
or anything the Democrats
need to call it --

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:38.770
because I'm not into names,
I'm into production.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.274
So, if I have
a steel wall --

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.709
or you could call it
a steel "fence."

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.377
We mentioned
the price that we want --

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:49.615
$5.6 billion --
very strongly.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.016
'Cause numbers
are thrown around.

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:53.085
You heard much
higher numbers.

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.287
Those higher numbers
were very much a misnomer.

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:57.423
You heard $20 billion
and $25 billion.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.193
-Yeah, that's true.
We did hear that --

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.427
from you.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.931
You told us it would cost
anywhere from $4 billion

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:07.033
to $20 billion,
Mexico would pay for it,

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.334
it would be a wall,
not a fence,

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:11.237
and you told a child
it would be made of concrete.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.771
Although, I'm sure
it's not the first time

00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:14.173
Trump has lied to a child.

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.307
[ As Trump ]
"Oh, no, of course, Eric.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.543
You're definitely
on the will."

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.011
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.247
[ Normal voice ] We are in a
self-inflicted political crisis

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:23.149
right now because Trump
made up something dumb,

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:25.717
didn't think it through, and
backed himself into a corner.

00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:27.986
He had two years of
total Republican control

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:29.354
to get it done,
and he didn't.

00:06:29.354 --> 00:06:31.423
And then, Democrats
took control of the House,

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:32.624
and Trump said...

00:06:32.624 --> 00:06:34.493
-Oh.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.995
This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:40.566
[ Cheers and applause ]

